using Lurp.Shared;

namespace Lurp.Storage;

/// <summary>
/// Single text source for the dead-candidate suppression ladder and response shape,
/// shared by the MCP tool description and the generated sections of <c>docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md</c>.
/// </summary>
public static class DeadCandidateLadder
{
    public const string Ladder =
        $"symbols of kind Type, Method, Property, Field, Event with no incoming LIVE edge (Calls, MethodGroupRef, Constructs, Reads, Writes, Handles, RoutesTo, Registers, MapsTo, MayDispatchTo, StaticallyCalls, TestedBy, ReflectionTypeRef, ReflectionMemberRef, ReflectionNameCandidate) of strong provenance (compiler_proved, framework_derived). Inherited liveness: accessors take their property's or event's edges by role (a getter every edge except Writes; a setter or init only Writes; an event accessor every edge of the event); type candidates also take these edges from outside the type: References, Returns, Inherits, Implements, Throws. A linked declaration also takes incoming edges from its copies in other projects, including when a project filter is set. Suppression ladder, in the order the store checks it: (1) a strong LIVE edge from outside the candidate -> alive, not a candidate. An edge never counts when its source is the candidate, an accessor of the candidate, the property or event of the candidate accessor or another accessor of it, or (for a type) a symbol inside the type; (2) the candidate overlaps a binding_incompleteness row of an unobservable reason (compiler_error, unresolved_metadata, ambiguous_overload, unsupported_syntax, extractor_failure, project_unreadable), or it is a non-abstract, non-static class or delegate (or an instance constructor of one) of an assembly that an unmodeled dependency injection scan names -> unresolved, reason binding_incompleteness; (3) the process entry point or the type that contains it (explicit static Main or the compiler-synthesized top-level-statements form; nothing in the repository calls it, whatever its accessibility) -> uncertain_dead, reason entry_point_convention; (4) implementation of an interface member or override of a member declared outside the compilation -> uncertain_dead, reason external_interface_implementation; (5) public surface: Public, Protected or protected internal by effective accessibility, which intersects declared accessibility with every containing type. Declared accessibility is used if effective accessibility is unavailable; an internal or private protected symbol of a project that grants InternalsVisibleTo to an assembly outside the snapshot (or to an assembly that the index cannot name) is public surface too -> excluded from proved_dead without include_public, uncertain_dead with reason public_surface when include_public is set; (6) a generated symbol (every declaration is in a generated document) with include_generated -> uncertain, reason generated_excluded; (7) symbol of a test project with include_tests -> uncertain, reason test_harness; (8) when the candidate has only weak incoming edges, the strongest weak edge decides: possible provenance -> uncertain_dead, reason possible_dispatch; convention provenance -> uncertain_dead, reason framework_convention; name_candidate provenance -> uncertain_dead, reason name_candidate; runtime_unknown provenance -> unresolved, reason runtime_unknown; (9) when the candidate has no incoming LIVE edge at all, its own convention verdict: EF mapping sources, fields and properties (including accessors) of mapped entities and their base types, and instance constructors of mapped entities and EF mapping source types -> uncertain_dead, reason ef_convention; a field, property or method with a serialization opt-in (such as JsonInclude, JsonProperty, DataMember, JsonConstructor, or a serialization callback attribute) -> uncertain_dead, reason serialization_convention; options binding members, unmodeled MediatR handler types and their constructors, and constructors of types activated by DI, MediatR or MVC -> uncertain_dead, reason framework_convention; then the inherited verdict (an accessor takes the verdict of its property, a type takes the first verdict among its members); (10) otherwise proved_dead, reason no_incoming_live_edges. Default excludes compiler-synthesized members (static constructors, implicitly declared members), extension-block marker types, generated symbols (every declaration is in a generated document) and test-project symbols (a project that references a test framework: {TestFrameworks.FrameworkAssembliesText}); lift with include_generated/include_tests (surfaced as uncertain reason generated_excluded/test_harness). Each call classifies the whole filtered universe with one batched incoming-edge query (WHERE target_symbol_id IN (...)) and cuts the page after classification, so the totals are exact; never one query per candidate. Liveness is one hop: a member reached only from a dead member is not a candidate.";

    public const string Response =
        "Response carries snapshot_id, filters, incoming_edge_kinds_checked[15], type_use_edge_kinds_checked[5], live_provenance_rank[2], uncertain_provenance[4], candidate_count (total filtered universe), dead_count/uncertain_count/unresolved_count (totals across all pages), candidates[] page window with symbol_id, fqn, kind, accessibility, effective_accessibility, document_path, locations[], project_name, declaration_count, is_generated, status (proved_dead/uncertain_dead/unresolved/uncertain), reason (handler-enum: no_incoming_live_edges, binding_incompleteness, public_surface, ef_convention, serialization_convention, framework_convention, possible_dispatch, name_candidate, runtime_unknown, generated_excluded, test_harness, entry_point_convention, external_interface_implementation), uncertainties[] (descriptions that state the same fact as a capsule uncertainty share its wording), incoming_edge_summary, declaration_span {start_line, end_line} (null when the symbol has no location), plus next_cursor and freshness.";

    public const string ToolDescription =
        $"List dead-code candidates for the pinned snapshot: {Ladder} {Response} Keyset pagination via limit/cursor ordered by symbol_id ASC; limit default 50 max 200.";
}
